WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.730
My guest this week is the American,

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:06.210
anti-gun violence
activist, Fred Guttenberg.

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.610
Fred's 14 year old daughter, Jaime,

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:12.180
was killed at her high
school alongside 16 others

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.400
by a teenage gunman.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.480
I want to talk to him

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.950
about how so many have become
desensitized to gun violence

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.320
and whether he thinks his great friend,

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.473
President Joe Biden, can
really tackle the issue.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.690
Fred thank you so much for being with me

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:44.070
and talking to all of us today.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.780
I really appreciate it.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.940
Thank you for having me on.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.210
I had to start by making sure,

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:54.300
we heard just something
about your daughter, Jaime,

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.630
first of all, because
this is why we're here

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.510
and I wanted to ask if you could be

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:03.310
as kind to tell us a little
bit about what she was like.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:10.370
My daughter was what every
parent would hope for

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:14.790
in a child.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:19.790
She was kind, she was
beautiful, she was decent,

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.330
she was tough, she was well-behaved.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.150
My daughter was a competitive dancer.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:30.750
That's how she spent
her time out of school

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.030
constantly practicing to dance.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:37.557
But what she also was is
somebody who understood

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:43.260
that not all kids had the same abilities.

00:01:46.502 --> 00:01:48.577
And so she dedicated her personal time,

00:01:48.577 --> 00:01:49.410
when she wasn't in school,
when she wasn't dancing

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:52.110
to volunteering for
different groups of kids

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.840
with differing abilities,
to make sure they had

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.030
all the same types of opportunities

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:59.703
for social connections
and for development.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:04.980
When she was in school,
she despised bullies,

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.610
and would put herself in the
middle of somebody bullying

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:11.433
and somebody being
bullied to make it stop.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:13.740
To the point, where as her dad,

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.640
I sometimes got real nervous about it,

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.530
but that's who she was, you know?

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:24.527
And I wasn't gonna stop her
from being that amazing person.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.420
She had her life figured out.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.790
She knew what she wanted going forward.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:33.090
She wanted to be a pediatric
physical therapist.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.400
She dreamt of working in a place called

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.440
The Paley Institute
where they do surgeries

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.150
on kids with limb deformities

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.520
to help a child walk for the first time.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:45.300
She wanted to be married
by the time she was 25.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.710
She had life figured out.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:47.763
She was amazing.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.370
She sounds like she had a lot figured out

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.470
and a lot of ambitions and hopes.

00:02:53.445 --> 00:02:58.445
And I suppose something
you have spoken about,

00:02:58.770 --> 00:02:59.730
and I know would be be a situation

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:01.410
any parent would find themselves in

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:02.760
if they were in your situation,

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.340
which sadly many parents are in America,

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.840
part of your work is looking at that.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:07.980
Yeah.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:11.580
Is you will have rerun that day many times

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:12.810
in your mind.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.880
If you don't mind me asking this as well,

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.750
I did wanna ask what you
remember about that morning.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.013
She went off to school.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.420
Well let's start

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.160
with the fact that it was Valentine's Day.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:27.840
February 14th.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.163
And it was a perfectly normal morning.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.330
And I say normal with
all the good and the bad.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:38.550
You know, the kids were
getting ready for school

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.020
and they were running late

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:43.530
and being siblings they
were blaming one another.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.970
My son was the driver.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:46.945
He was gonna drive them both.

00:03:46.945 --> 00:03:49.320
And because they were running late,

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.990
I was rushing them out the door

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:54.600
and I kept on telling them,
'you've gotta go, you gotta go.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.810
You're gonna be late,
you gotta get to school'.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.340
And those were the last words

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:02.314
to my two children that morning.

00:04:02.314 --> 00:04:05.135
My last words to my son and my daughter

00:04:05.135 --> 00:04:07.560
that morning were not, 'I love you'.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.960
It was, 'you've gotta go,
you're gonna be late'.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:11.850
I was sending them to school.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:16.850
I never expected that later
that day I would find out

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.020
I would never get the chance again

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:22.020
to tell my daughter how much I love her.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:24.090
But I didn't do it that morning.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:26.580
And it is something I will live with

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:28.590
for the rest of my life.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:30.810
It is the reason why I tell every parent

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:33.360
and everybody who loves somebody else

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.400
to make sure you never missed a chance

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:39.030
to look someone in the eye and
tell them eyeball to eyeball

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:40.620
how much you love them.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:44.220
'Cause you never know when you
won't get that chance again.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:45.810
It's such an important message.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:48.360
Thank you for sharing that Fred.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:50.220
I really appreciate it and-

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.420
Thank you.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.250
You are then in your day,

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:57.360
it's February 14th and going
about your business as usual.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.100
Yeah.
And how do you learn

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.600
something is wrong?

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.860
Is there a phone call?

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.023
How does this knowledge
start to reach you?

00:05:05.741 --> 00:05:09.803
Just after 2pm, I get a
phone call from my son

00:05:09.803 --> 00:05:12.360
and, you know, kids in school
today have cell phones,

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.483
so there's regular communication
throughout the day.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.870
And my son calls me just after 2

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.120
and he was a bit of a jokester.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.340
So he calls and he says,

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.203
'dad there's a shooting at my school'.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:29.820
My initial instinct was 'what
the heck is he talking about?'

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:31.980
You know, that's a weird
thing to make a joke about

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:34.230
but what is he talking about?

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:37.830
But he immediately, you then
said 'and I can't find Jaime'.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.890
Now my son looked after
his sister like a hawk.

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:43.140
He would never play games with her safety.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:44.700
And then the second he said that

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:47.718
I knew this wasn't a
joke and he was serious.

00:05:47.718 --> 00:05:50.538
And so I said to him, 'where are you?'

00:05:50.538 --> 00:05:53.760
And he said, 'they're making us all run,

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:55.950
but I can't find Jaime'.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.540
And I said, 'you need to run'.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.310
He goes, 'but I can't find Jamie'.

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:02.460
He kept saying it to me over and over

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:05.670
and telling me he wants
to turn around and go

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.770
to where they know the
shooting was happening

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:09.150
in which that building.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:11.160
And I'm like, 'you can't do that.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:12.240
You need to run.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.340
I'll worry about your sister'.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.950
And as I'm on the phone with
him and he's crying to me

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:20.516
that he can't find his sister,

00:06:20.516 --> 00:06:21.349
there's gunshots.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.180
As I'm on the phone with him,

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.920
it's the shots on the third floor

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:28.323
it's the shots that
were killing his sister.

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:31.830
He listened to them and I listened to them

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:32.663
on the phone while I was

00:06:33.671 --> 00:06:34.740
speaking to him,

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.153
convincing him to run.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:39.243
Because of those shots,

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:42.240
I was able to finally convince him

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:45.360
to keep just running as far
from that noise as he could.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:46.983
And he made it to safety.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:50.730
Unfortunately, the rest of that afternoon

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:54.723
was all about my wife and I
trying to find our daughter,

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:57.450
hoping she was okay,

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.490
hoping the fact that we
couldn't reach her was only

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:02.070
because maybe she dropped her phone

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:04.710
and eventually she'd call us
from somebody else's phone.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:07.170
It was getting to the hospital,

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:08.003
so that we could

00:07:09.045 --> 00:07:10.050
try to find her there

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:13.233
hoping she was now injured
and couldn't reach us.

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:15.653
And it wasn't until,

00:07:16.528 --> 00:07:17.369
you know,

00:07:17.369 --> 00:07:18.202
around 5:30-ish

00:07:19.594 --> 00:07:21.210
when we learned

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:23.910
through a friend of mine
who was a police officer

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:25.743
that she was shot and killed.

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:28.143
I'm so sorry.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:31.050
Thank you.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.583
I really am. And

00:07:33.583 --> 00:07:34.983
apart from all

00:07:34.983 --> 00:07:36.174
the things

00:07:36.174 --> 00:07:37.007
that will come

00:07:37.007 --> 00:07:41.531
with such devastation, your
life really changed that day

00:07:41.531 --> 00:07:42.900
in completely other way

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.210
because of how we're speaking now,

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:48.415
which is part of your message.
Yeah.

00:07:48.415 --> 00:07:51.265
You, you suddenly found yourself

00:07:51.265 --> 00:07:54.900
in a position where you
knew about the violence,

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:56.880
the gun violence, the
mass shootings in America

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:58.440
but you obviously until that point

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:02.310
hadn't known about them
in quite the same way.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:04.773
And you find yourself with a cause.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:07.853
Listen, I live with this

00:08:09.578 --> 00:08:11.220
intense guilt

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:15.543
that my voice wasn't a part of
this before it was my family.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.410
I'll never get over that.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:22.860
But it's a part of this cause now.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:27.840
The crazy thing is it
didn't happen immediately.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.050
The first 24 hours are,
were actually a blur,

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:33.360
while I knew my daughter was killed

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:36.030
I hadn't really started to focus

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:38.910
on the notion that this was gun violence

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:41.400
until the next day at night

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:43.860
when I went to the Parkland vigil.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:46.770
And at that vigil the
mayor asked if I wanted

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.592
to take her speaking slot

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:51.810
and I hadn't prepared anything

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:54.427
but I said, you know, what the heck?

00:08:54.427 --> 00:08:57.547
And I went up there and I
looked at this crowd of people

00:08:57.547 --> 00:09:01.410
thousands of people crying
with candles and lights.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.420
And that was the moment where it hit me

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:06.870
that this was a gun violence

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:09.720
that broke my family,
that broke my community.

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:12.270
And I just remember telling people

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:14.580
that vigil about my daughter

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.560
but saying to everyone in the crowd,

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:21.480
'this time gun violence
came to the wrong family

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.360
to the wrong dad and to
the wrong community'.

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:26.001
And

00:09:26.001 --> 00:09:29.220
I went home that night
and I walked in my house

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:31.140
and I said to my family and friends

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:33.630
who were there who didn't go to the vigil,

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:35.583
I'm gonna break that effing gun lobby.

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:38.730
And it's been my mission ever since,

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:42.030
is to break that lobby
and to break their grip

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:46.200
on our legislators and
getting effective legislation

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:49.650
to do something about
gun violence in America.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:50.991
And

00:09:50.991 --> 00:09:52.800
I can't stop.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.960
Well, there are many people
who are very grateful

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:57.030
to you because they would also say

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.800
that they would be scared
to do it, you know,

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.720
because of the carrying of guns

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:02.820
and because of the threats,
because of the risk.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:04.380
Sure.
Are you ever scared

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:06.930
to speak up and and say anything

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:08.670
'cause of what's happened
to your family as well?

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:09.503
Yeah.

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:14.220
Well, because of what
happened to my family

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:17.373
I've lost this capacity for fear.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.640
What my daughter had,

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.520
running down the hallway
with an active shooter

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:26.280
carrying an AR-15 at her back.

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:29.400
You know, people need to
remember, my daughter knew

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:32.220
it wasn't like she was caught by surprise.

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:34.110
She knew what she was running from.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:35.640
She was in the hallway,

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:37.860
she was the second to last to be shot.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:40.533
She made it to within
one second of safety.

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:44.193
What she had was fear.

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:48.870
Genuine, real fear that
I'll never ever fully

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:52.740
be able to understand or comprehend.

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:56.943
And because I'll never have
the level of fear that she had,

00:10:57.810 --> 00:11:01.113
you can't intimidate me anymore.

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:04.743
You can't. Words won't do it.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:10.110
What I really have found more than that

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:13.680
is the majority of people in this country

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:18.300
have been supportive, have
been amazing, and give me hope

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:23.130
because the majority of people
in this country are like me.

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:25.710
It's not that they're anti-gun,

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:27.780
it's they're anti-gun violence.

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:30.962
They want to do something about that.

00:11:30.962 --> 00:11:35.962
And so for every person who
tries to intimidate or threaten,

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:39.780
I can genuinely say 'I don't care'.

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:44.472
But to everybody who understands

00:11:44.472 --> 00:11:45.538
what my mission is

00:11:45.538 --> 00:11:49.950
and is supportive, I can
genuinely say 'thank you'.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:52.320
And I hear you because I do.

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:54.370
And yet what you said

00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:56.670
and I'm very struck by
it, I'm moved by it.

00:11:56.670 --> 00:11:58.537
Where you said at the beginning

00:11:58.537 --> 00:12:00.330
of our conversation that you have guilt

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:04.110
about not adding your voice before.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.060
It doesn't mean you didn't care.

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:07.560
It's about something else

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:08.850
which I wanted to get your view on

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:10.300
which is

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.360
how do you get people to care

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:14.760
to the point where they
also push for change?

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:18.300
Or rather, how do you stop
people from being desensitized

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:21.720
to this because it's so common,
gun violence in America.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.463
Yeah.
How do you do that?

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:26.217
You know, it's such a great question

00:12:26.217 --> 00:12:29.610
and I look back and
I'll just use Sandy Hook

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:30.633
as an example.

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:36.270
I felt horrible emotion
over it, anger over it.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:40.410
I watched all the news reporting
over it and I did nothing.

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:41.243
I did nothing.

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:45.180
And I lived in this bubble.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:47.100
I mean this was Parkland, Florida.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.720
This was the community,

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:49.898
actually a lot like Newtown

00:12:49.898 --> 00:12:52.249
where you never see this happening.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:54.383
And

00:12:55.683 --> 00:12:59.323
I allowed myself to stay in this bubble,

00:12:59.323 --> 00:13:02.836
part of what I do now to help people care.

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:06.205
People always say to me,

00:13:06.205 --> 00:13:08.430
'I can't imagine how you feel'.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:11.880
I go out of my way every chance I get

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:14.520
to help people imagine how I feel,

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:17.700
to help people imagine the terror,

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.950
to help people imagine the violence,

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:23.880
and to help people imagine
themselves in that.

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:28.020
And not me, because I think
at the end of the day,

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:29.610
the more people realize

00:13:29.610 --> 00:13:32.910
while this happened to somebody else,

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:35.490
but it could happen to
me when I go to the mall,

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:37.920
it could happen to me when
I go to the shopping center

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:39.120
or the movies.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:42.150
It could happen to my family
when I send them to school,

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:47.150
the more likely they are to
become part of solving it.

00:13:47.195 --> 00:13:50.228
And I will tell you, if you
look at the last three elections

00:13:50.228 --> 00:13:53.430
in this country, doing
something about gun violence

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.330
has been a top voting issue.

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:58.250
It has changed election outcomes.

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:00.115
And I think people are listening now.

00:14:00.115 --> 00:14:03.000
And if you look at polls,

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:06.900
over 80% of America wants to solve this.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.643
We are winning the fight,

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:11.970
but moving the political system

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:14.640
in this country is a lot of work.

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:16.110
Well, I mean you say that as well,

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:19.140
but I'm also aware that
we've seen recently in states

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:20.700
where there have been mass shootings

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:24.030
politicians reelected who
are anti-gun reform as well.

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:26.370
I mean there is that reality,

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:28.650
they may have been voted
for for other policies.

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:31.410
Politics is not a one
policy thing of course.

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:35.400
But you've spoken very
publicly about your bond

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:37.650
with the president, with Joe Biden.

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:39.000
Yeah.
I know that he was

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.920
an important figure for you

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:43.260
and a relationship you
say you wouldn't have

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:45.960
without what happened
to you and your family.

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:50.190
But do you have faith that
he can be the president

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:52.230
to make that change?

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:54.480
Because, you know, there
isn't that much longer left

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:57.030
in some ways and we dunno
what's gonna happen next.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:03.330
Without question, not
only do I have faith,

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:05.670
I can actually point to the fact

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:08.250
that something has
already been accomplished

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:11.730
that is historic and hasn't
happened in over 30 years,

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:15.240
which was back in April he
signed the Safer Communities Act,

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:19.740
a real piece of gun violence
prevention legislation

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:23.100
that does really big things

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:26.250
to start to finally bend the curve

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:28.050
and reduce gun violence.

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:30.300
Is it everything I could have hoped for?

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:32.610
Is it everything I would've wanted?

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:35.130
Well, no, it's not.

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:38.370
But, it was a real significant package

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:42.090
that was able to get bipartisan support.

00:15:42.090 --> 00:15:46.650
And I'm actually, to this day,

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:50.130
so thankful for his leadership on that,

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:52.320
for the leadership of
people like my friend

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:57.320
Senator Chris Murphy, who
negotiated in the Senate

00:15:57.480 --> 00:16:00.150
nonstop to get it done.

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:02.550
Even when, and he will tell you this,

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:06.240
I didn't have faith that
he could get it done.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:09.390
I never saw him being able to accomplish

00:16:09.390 --> 00:16:12.540
in the Senate what he
did, but he got it done.

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:16.350
But Fred, there's been
more violence since,

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:18.570
there's been more shootings.
Sure.

00:16:18.570 --> 00:16:20.370
How do we move or how do you

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:24.540
and the people you are working
with move to stop that?

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.430
What needs to change?

00:16:26.430 --> 00:16:30.218
Well, listen, and it's a great question.

00:16:30.218 --> 00:16:33.038
If, you know, we passed
this back in April.

00:16:33.038 --> 00:16:36.960
If you look back to when my
daughter was killed in 2018,

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:39.420
there were about 300
million weapons in America.

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:42.090
By the time we passed this legislation

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:45.270
there were 400 million
weapons and ghost guns.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:48.378
So the reality is we haven't,

00:16:50.836 --> 00:16:51.990
you know,

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:55.770
the legislation passed is
gonna be forward looking

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:58.500
and I believe will have
a real dramatic impact.

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:00.690
Right.
But we have to come to grips

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:04.260
with the reality of the numbers
of weapons that we have.

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:07.020
I will tell you for me personally,

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:10.440
the Holy Grail of solving
gun violence in America

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:12.619
at this point, because
of the numbers of guns

00:17:12.619 --> 00:17:14.713
that are out there, is through ammunition.

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:19.710
And I am working to pass something

00:17:19.710 --> 00:17:23.310
in the United States
Congress called Jamie's Law

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:26.970
which seeks to extend
background checks to ammunition.

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:29.820
There's no requirement for a
background check on ammunition.

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:32.160
So, you have all these weapons out there,

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:33.810
many of which are in the hands of people

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:36.540
who are what's called
a prohibited purchaser.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:38.400
So they have to get their gun illegally,

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:40.770
or they steal it or they trade for it,

00:17:40.770 --> 00:17:43.680
and they walk right into the
store and buy the bullets.

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:48.680
If we can get background checks
on ammunition, we stop that.

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:50.760
We'll save lives immediately.

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:54.420
And so for me, that's
the Holy Grail right now

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:55.710
of solving this problem.

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:57.330
And I'm not gonna stop.

00:17:57.330 --> 00:17:58.440
That's fascinating.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:01.350
It makes a lot of sense because
of what's already in play,

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:03.810
like you talk about and, you know,

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.130
we will see what happens

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:08.868
because it's so political
and it's such a strong lobby.

00:18:08.868 --> 00:18:11.070
Yeah.

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:14.130
This is a very simplistic way

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:15.698
of asking something quite complex.

00:18:15.698 --> 00:18:18.030
But, because you've
looked at this so much,

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:21.660
who do you blame for
your daughter's killing?

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:22.493
Hmm.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.380
A lot of people.

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:30.380
Let's start with all of
those who failed to stop it

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:34.803
when they had different chances to do so.

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:40.113
Let's start with the person
who made the decision to do it,

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:41.933
but also

00:18:43.875 --> 00:18:48.874
I can not focus on the political reality

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:54.213
that we live in a country
where that killer,

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:59.550
in spite of all the red flags,
was able to buy the gun.

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:04.470
And so I do blame the
legislators who failed

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:07.890
to do anything meaningful
for all of the years.

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:12.330
I look at, just my
daughter was born in 2003.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:15.420
The year she was born
there was actually a ban

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:19.593
on assault weapons in
America that expired in 2004.

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:25.380
And you can look at
the trajectory of sales

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:27.423
after that ban expired.

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:30.807
You then fast forward to 2007

00:19:30.807 --> 00:19:33.840
and the Heller Supreme Court decision,

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:36.998
which put in place this whole

00:19:38.031 --> 00:19:41.188
phrasing around common use.

00:19:41.188 --> 00:19:46.188
And the industry built common
use into a business model.

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:50.550
And they kept on manufacturing
and flooding our streets

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:53.460
with more and more and more
of these weapons every year

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:57.480
to the point where they were
no longer just being used

00:19:57.480 --> 00:20:00.300
from a hunting or sport perspective.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:03.540
They were now being used overwhelmingly

00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:07.470
in daily violent incidents.

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:12.470
So I blame everybody who's a part of

00:20:12.545 --> 00:20:14.378
building that system,

00:20:14.378 --> 00:20:16.680
whether it's the Supreme Court decision,

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:18.750
whether it's all the legislators

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:20.970
who failed to do anything to prevent

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:24.360
this explosion of weapons on our streets.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:25.890
I blame them all.

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:29.640
And those legislators who still exist,

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:33.150
who refuse to acknowledge the significance

00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:38.150
of this problem and who
fight back and who use BS,

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:42.243
you know lies, to continue
to push that system.

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:45.120
They have blood on their hands right now.

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:47.198
I blame them right now.

00:20:47.198 --> 00:20:52.198
And so, stopping the next
one requires defeating

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:56.703
still more people and we're
gonna continue working to do it.

00:20:57.600 --> 00:21:00.540
You mentioned right at
the top of that list,

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:02.650
unsurprisingly, rightly, the killer

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:06.780
who hasn't been given the death sentence.

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:09.690
Instead, it's life in jail.

00:21:09.690 --> 00:21:12.598
What was your reaction to
that quite recent decision?

00:21:15.360 --> 00:21:17.863
For the past almost five years now,

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:23.080
my life has really been very much

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:27.480
wrapped around what's gonna happen to him

00:21:27.480 --> 00:21:30.240
and the trial and that outcome.

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:33.540
And, because there was
gonna be this trial,

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:36.240
I wanted him to get the
ultimate punishment.

00:21:36.240 --> 00:21:38.853
I wanted him to get the death sentence.

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:44.790
And when the verdict was delivered,

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:49.533
for a couple of days, I was
actually very distraught.

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:52.440
But then I went to visit my daughter

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:56.280
at the cemetery and I always come back

00:21:56.280 --> 00:22:01.280
from a visit with her,
maybe, feeling smarter,

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:05.340
because in her own way,
she communicates with me.

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:08.070
And I left the cemetery and I realized

00:22:08.070 --> 00:22:10.680
no matter what happened to the killer,

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:11.610
every day going forward

00:22:11.610 --> 00:22:14.010
I'm still gonna be visiting
my daughter at the cemetery.

00:22:14.010 --> 00:22:17.790
Nothing changed, nothing changes.

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:21.120
And it put me in a place

00:22:21.120 --> 00:22:24.540
where I was finally able to
put the killer out of my head.

00:22:24.540 --> 00:22:26.700
He got the punishment he got.

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:29.850
He's going to one of the most
miserable places on earth

00:22:29.850 --> 00:22:31.900
in the Florida Department of Corrections.

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:36.753
He will face ultimate
judgment there I'm sure.

00:22:38.160 --> 00:22:41.100
But I'll still be visiting
my daughter at the cemetery.

00:22:41.100 --> 00:22:44.970
And because of that, it was in that moment

00:22:44.970 --> 00:22:48.330
where I was finally able to
put that killer out of my head.

00:22:48.330 --> 00:22:50.280
He's no longer in my head.

00:22:50.280 --> 00:22:52.650
I no longer think about him.

00:22:52.650 --> 00:22:55.590
I no longer wonder what's
gonna happen to him.

00:22:55.590 --> 00:22:57.607
I no longer

00:22:57.607 --> 00:23:01.357
have any second or minute

00:23:01.357 --> 00:23:04.950
of my time focused on him.

00:23:04.950 --> 00:23:07.350
I'm no longer losing sleep over him.

00:23:07.350 --> 00:23:09.993
And so while I was
disappointed in the verdict,

00:23:12.150 --> 00:23:15.030
I'm actually now in a healthier place

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:16.880
than I've been for almost five years.

00:23:18.150 --> 00:23:21.570
Well that's very good to
hear and important as well

00:23:21.570 --> 00:23:24.963
because the only thing we can
control are our reactions.

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:27.180
Yeah.
I'm also just aware,

00:23:27.180 --> 00:23:30.690
picking up what we were talking
a little bit about before

00:23:30.690 --> 00:23:32.700
that we still, amazingly,

00:23:32.700 --> 00:23:34.890
and I say that in the
true sense of the word,

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:37.680
have people who write horrific things

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:40.410
about these mass shootings,
who don't believe them.

00:23:40.410 --> 00:23:42.033
Conspiracy theorists.

00:23:43.200 --> 00:23:46.383
You'll be very familiar
with this terrain, sadly.

00:23:47.340 --> 00:23:49.233
What do you think of Alex Jones?

00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:52.860
I think Alex Jones

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:57.180
is the lowest form of
humanity that exists.

00:23:57.180 --> 00:24:01.950
I wish him nothing but terrible outcomes

00:24:01.950 --> 00:24:06.780
because of what he did to other
people and continues to do,

00:24:06.780 --> 00:24:09.840
you know, in spite of these horrible,

00:24:09.840 --> 00:24:12.063
financial legal judgments against him,

00:24:12.930 --> 00:24:14.943
he hasn't stopped behaving badly.

00:24:16.740 --> 00:24:18.360
He is a liar.

00:24:18.360 --> 00:24:22.980
He is somebody who has
directed violence at others.

00:24:22.980 --> 00:24:27.980
He has used his platform
not for good, but for evil.

00:24:28.620 --> 00:24:33.420
And so in his remaining days on earth,

00:24:33.420 --> 00:24:37.710
I hope he pays a horrible price

00:24:37.710 --> 00:24:41.790
directed by the courts and
pursued by those families

00:24:41.790 --> 00:24:44.733
that he spent all those years harassing.

00:24:45.810 --> 00:24:50.400
And I am certain that when his time is up,

00:24:50.400 --> 00:24:53.743
he will pay a final judgment as well.

00:24:55.065 --> 00:24:58.593
He is as low a form of
human life as can exist.

00:25:00.060 --> 00:25:02.220
You talk about use of platform.

00:25:02.220 --> 00:25:05.400
I also noticed that when
the new owner of Twitter

00:25:05.400 --> 00:25:09.660
the other day, Elon Musk,
posted a photo recently

00:25:09.660 --> 00:25:13.560
of a bedside table cans of Diet Coke.

00:25:13.560 --> 00:25:15.810
Also a gun, actually
transpired to be a toy gun

00:25:15.810 --> 00:25:17.010
which I didn't realize at the time.

00:25:17.010 --> 00:25:19.380
Sure.
You chose to post-

00:25:19.380 --> 00:25:22.530
It actually doesn't matter
whether it was real or not

00:25:22.530 --> 00:25:25.680
because the message he
was trying to deliver

00:25:25.680 --> 00:25:26.550
is what matters.

00:25:26.550 --> 00:25:27.383
Yeah.

00:25:27.383 --> 00:25:28.713
I just meant I didn't know.

00:25:28.713 --> 00:25:29.700
Yeah.
You know, but it was

00:25:29.700 --> 00:25:31.440
a very striking image.
Sure.

00:25:31.440 --> 00:25:35.490
You posted in response to that

00:25:35.490 --> 00:25:37.740
talking about the fact that
your daughter was killed.

00:25:37.740 --> 00:25:39.240
The everyday children are killed

00:25:39.240 --> 00:25:41.343
because of irresponsible adults.

00:25:43.255 --> 00:25:46.055
What do you feel about that
having also reflected on it?

00:25:49.080 --> 00:25:54.080
It's so strange now
watching what Elon Musk

00:25:54.240 --> 00:25:56.220
is turning himself into.

00:25:56.220 --> 00:26:00.660
He is a business person
who I was mesmerized by

00:26:00.660 --> 00:26:04.743
for so many years who I
thought did the coolest things.

00:26:05.640 --> 00:26:10.640
And if he had a vision,
I automatically thought

00:26:10.920 --> 00:26:15.120
if Elon Musk thinks he can pull
it off, I'll bet you he can.

00:26:15.120 --> 00:26:19.560
I looked at him that way
until his pursuit of Twitter

00:26:19.560 --> 00:26:22.620
and what he's turned it
into which is a cesspool

00:26:22.620 --> 00:26:26.100
of indecency and the worst of humanity.

00:26:26.100 --> 00:26:30.753
And that photo that he
posted is just an example.

00:26:31.740 --> 00:26:34.980
He was, for whatever reason,

00:26:34.980 --> 00:26:37.800
he felt important to post this image

00:26:37.800 --> 00:26:40.260
of guns by the side of his bed.

00:26:40.260 --> 00:26:44.250
I spend my life, every day, trying to talk

00:26:44.250 --> 00:26:47.793
about responsible gun ownership
and locking weapons up.

00:26:48.930 --> 00:26:52.590
Two of my dear friends, people
who I wish I didn't know,

00:26:52.590 --> 00:26:54.450
but I do because of gun violence.

00:26:54.450 --> 00:26:55.740
Mike and Kristin Song,

00:26:55.740 --> 00:27:00.343
their son Ethan was killed
because of an unlocked weapon.

00:27:00.343 --> 00:27:05.343
And so I don't care that
that wasn't a real weapon,

00:27:05.343 --> 00:27:07.860
'cause he didn't say that in his message.

00:27:07.860 --> 00:27:10.470
He implied he's keeping
these unlocked weapons

00:27:10.470 --> 00:27:11.757
by the side of his bed.

00:27:11.757 --> 00:27:13.710
And I find that dangerous.

00:27:13.710 --> 00:27:16.530
And I find that encouraging to others

00:27:16.530 --> 00:27:19.773
to do dumb, stupid, irresponsible things.

00:27:20.790 --> 00:27:25.290
Why he's pursuing this
path in his life now?

00:27:25.290 --> 00:27:29.048
Why he's behaving like the richest troll

00:27:30.414 --> 00:27:31.256
on earth

00:27:31.256 --> 00:27:33.780
instead of this successful business person

00:27:33.780 --> 00:27:36.120
that he had previously been?

00:27:36.120 --> 00:27:39.900
I can't make sense of,
but I hope he fails.

00:27:39.900 --> 00:27:41.250
Well we'll see how that transpires

00:27:41.250 --> 00:27:43.470
in terms of that platform and the owner,

00:27:43.470 --> 00:27:46.440
ownership of that business
and perhaps also what changes

00:27:46.440 --> 00:27:48.600
are or are not made.

00:27:48.600 --> 00:27:49.625
Just finally,

00:27:51.216 --> 00:27:55.093
what do you think Jaime would
make of what you're doing

00:27:55.093 --> 00:27:58.620
and your fight and how
you're going about it?

00:27:58.620 --> 00:27:59.453
You know, it's funny,

00:27:59.453 --> 00:28:03.693
my wife and I have had numerous
conversations about that.

00:28:05.670 --> 00:28:10.670
On one hand, she would
be completely embarrassed

00:28:11.250 --> 00:28:13.080
by the attention.

00:28:13.080 --> 00:28:15.788
'Cause while my daughter

00:28:17.196 --> 00:28:19.321
was always out there

00:28:19.321 --> 00:28:22.500
and performing, she was
still a shy little kid,

00:28:22.500 --> 00:28:26.493
and she would be completely
embarrassed by the attention.

00:28:27.840 --> 00:28:30.270
On the other hand, in my home,

00:28:30.270 --> 00:28:34.192
my wife and my son are
very different than me.

00:28:34.192 --> 00:28:39.192
They were never as into the news

00:28:39.758 --> 00:28:42.666
and politics the way I was.

00:28:42.666 --> 00:28:44.040
But Jaime was.

00:28:44.040 --> 00:28:47.340
Jaime was the one who would
sit with me and watch.

00:28:47.340 --> 00:28:50.280
And when I would get angry
at things that were happening

00:28:50.280 --> 00:28:53.940
or uplifted by things that were
happening, she was with me.

00:28:53.940 --> 00:28:55.830
She was participating.

00:28:55.830 --> 00:28:59.954
And so Jaime, because of that,

00:28:59.954 --> 00:29:02.046
and because of her toughness

00:29:02.046 --> 00:29:05.283
because of her dislike of bullies,

00:29:06.270 --> 00:29:09.690
because of her concern for others,

00:29:09.690 --> 00:29:12.480
she would be, on the
one hand, embarrassed.

00:29:12.480 --> 00:29:14.400
But on the other hand,
I know she would have

00:29:14.400 --> 00:29:18.903
her hands on my back
saying 'go dad, do this'.

00:29:20.070 --> 00:29:21.690
Let's save the next one.

00:29:21.690 --> 00:29:23.580
She sounds like my kind of girl

00:29:23.580 --> 00:29:26.460
getting very into it
her news, her politics

00:29:26.460 --> 00:29:27.540
and trying to, you know,

00:29:27.540 --> 00:29:30.030
stand up I suppose for what she believes.

00:29:30.030 --> 00:29:32.730
Thank you so much for telling us about her

00:29:32.730 --> 00:29:35.850
and also your work today.
Thank you.

00:29:35.850 --> 00:29:38.613
I really appreciate the
time and the insights.

00:29:39.540 --> 00:29:40.767
Thank you.

00:29:40.767 --> 00:29:43.440
And thank you so much for being with us.

00:29:43.440 --> 00:29:46.636
Until we meet again, do
take care and goodbye.

